@strong{@anchor{Exercise 0.4}Exercise 0.4:} Extend the section's
@code{Shape} with a third variant, @code{Square}, carrying one side, and
write @code{area} as an exhaustive @code{switch} over all three variants.
Then run the compile experiment: delete the @code{Square} case, run
@command{just lint}, record the compiler's message, restore the case, and
say in one sentence what the exhaustiveness check bought you. The tests
pin all three areas: a circle of radius 1 has area @code{Math.PI}, a
2-by-3 rectangle has area 6, and a square of side 4 has area 16.

